      "rawRetained": true,
      "reason": "The multi-catch handles failed cleanup of a previously captured management owner. A direct cleanup Error supersedes an ordinary Runtime primary; an already selected primary Error remains first. The second instanceof prevents replacing the original fatal identity. Non-promoted cleanup contributes only a fixed preallocated secondary diagnostic unless it is the same object. stopFailure returning an unconfirmed result does not make start succeed: the original failure is thrown. Splitting or deleting the checks merely to silence PMD can change cleanup/primary order. Actual listener/executor cleanup, suppressed graphs and native owner termination remain unqualified.",
